From 1556992ada2df2d96f24395be28664c9f8194a83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 13:20:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: the Failover tab's health-check text no longer points at
 a check "above"

Owner, 2026-09-07. RDHC_2 opened with "Not the ASUS check above, which resolves
a name through the router to decide whether the internet is up" - written while
the block sat on the System page beside the ASUS Network Monitoring row. On its
own tab there is no check above it to contrast with, so the sentence now simply
states what that resolution is: "Resolves a name through the router to decide
whether the internet is up." The rest of the paragraph is unchanged.

The first sentence only, in all 25 packs (the remainder of every translation is
byte-identical); lockstep holds. The guide's 4.14a paragraph loses the same
stale "beside the ASUS Network Monitoring row" clause.

Gates: reaper_static_checks 11/11. The token sits in an HTML text context
(<p><#RDHC_2#></p>), never a JS string, so no pack can break the page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
